{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1791900000000-architect-srvm-amendments-review-r2.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-11 07:00:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-11 14:00:00 Asia/Bangkok\n\n# Task: confirm the amendment fixes (round 2, continuing your thread)\n\nRead-only. Worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-amend, branch srvm-amend, HEAD 71eab563 (fixes on top of 695c3ec0; git diff 695c3ec0 HEAD). Fable's report: collab/1791890000000-architect-srvm-amendments-fix.report.md.\n\nConfirm each of your five round-1 findings is fixed correctly: (1) frozen section 7 and UCF 7.3.2 precedence; (2) carrier step 7 calls frame/task-defect per body first (halted bodies included); (3) free-env in BOTH root lists (carrier census and UCF fixed-point) consistent with continuation design 7.1; (4) code-as-tuples 7.1, impact table and UCF matrix: two AST lanes plus direct vector load, no instruction-vector projection acceptance; (5) A7->A2 (including the one permitted edit in the continuation companion design), qualified frozen 8.4 references, BLAKE3 spellings. Re-grep all five amended documents for the residue classes (legacy reader requirements, semantic-only gates, unchanged-profile claims, no-kernel-translation, vector-to-datoms loading, stack-cref/:regs/:kframe/stack-base carrier rows, v3-stamp-does-not-move, :segment/sha256- spellings, re-version/b3/r3 language) and report any remaining operative occurrence. Do not reopen settled items.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS Asia/Bangkok>\nThen findings (severity | file:line | evidence | correction), per-item answers, and end with exactly one line:\nVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE | CHANGES_REQUESTED\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
